# CODEOWNERS
# Paths are matched from the repository root. The last matching pattern wins.
#
# NOTE: the @owner values below are placeholders pointing at the organisation. Replace
# them with real GitHub handles or teams before turning on required review. A CODEOWNERS
# rule that matches nobody provides no protection while looking like it does.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
/*                       @dip-develop

# Specification and architecture: changes here change the contract for every package.
/docs/                   @dip-develop
/ARCHITECTURE.md         @dip-develop

# Security-sensitive material. Treat every PR touching these as security-relevant and
# require a reviewer other than the author.
/SECURITY.md                  @dip-develop
/docs/security/               @dip-develop
/docs/extensibility/plugins.md @dip-develop
/docs/extensibility/tools.md   @dip-develop
/docs/decisions/risks.md      @dip-develop

# Compatibility surfaces: protocol framing, config schema, error and exit codes.
/docs/architecture/protocol.md      @dip-develop
/docs/architecture/configuration.md @dip-develop
/docs/reference/                    @dip-develop

# Release, signing and automation.
/.github/workflows/   @dip-develop
/.github/dependabot.yml @dip-develop

# The lockfile is committed deliberately: one reviewer, no drive-by updates.
/pubspec.lock         @dip-develop
